# ============================================================================
# Config moved to env/  (2026-07-12) — see env/README.md
#
# The environment is now split into topical files so you only touch what you need:
#   env/app.env          app behaviour · feature flags · model tiers · universe · knobs
#   env/gemini.env       GOOGLE_API_KEY (the one Gemini key)
#   env/data-keys.env    data-source API keys (OpenDART · ECOS · FRED · FMP · KIS · KRX · …)
#   env/auth-billing.env social login · email OTP · Toss billing · alert channels
#   env/secrets.env      generated prod secrets (AUTH_SECRET · SERVICE_TOKEN · ADMIN_TOKEN · …)
#
# Set up:
#   for f in env/*.env.example; do cp "$f" "${f%.example}"; done   # then fill them in
#   # or, if you already have a monolithic .env:  bash scripts/split_env.sh
#
# Each env/*.env.example is the annotated reference for its variables.
#
# BACK-COMPAT: a single root .env STILL WORKS — docker compose reads it alongside the
# env/ files (all optional; env/* override .env). So an existing .env keeps the stack
# running unchanged; migrate to env/ whenever you like.
# ============================================================================
#
# ⚠️ COMPOSE INTERPOLATION VARIABLES — these MUST live HERE (root .env) or the shell,
# NOT in env/*.env. docker compose substitutes ${VAR} in the compose file (ports, etc.)
# ONLY from the root .env / shell; env/*.env are `env_file:` entries that are injected
# INTO containers and are invisible to interpolation. Putting these in env/app.env does
# nothing to the host port bind.
#
# Expose the admin console (:8005) on the network (default is 127.0.0.1 loopback, SC-0.2).
# The console has CRUD over every service DB — prefer restricting source IPs at your cloud
# firewall over 0.0.0.0/0. After changing this you MUST recreate: `docker compose up -d admin`.
# ADMIN_BIND=0.0.0.0
# App-level source-IP allowlist (comma-separated IPs/CIDRs). EMPTY = allow all (default).
# ADMINUI_IP_ALLOWLIST=203.0.113.5/32,10.0.0.0/8
# Admin login (defaults admin/admin — change for any non-loopback exposure):
# ADMINUI_USERNAME=admin
# ADMINUI_PASSWORD=change-me
